Use the backend API through its configured Render service URL. Do not call Gemini
directly from the browser or place a provider API key in frontend code.

Set BACKEND_URL to the Render service origin and use an email/password you control:

1. Register or sign in:

curl.exe -X POST "%BACKEND_URL%/api/v1/auth/login" ^
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" ^
  --data-raw "{\"email\":\"<your-email>\",\"password\":\"<your-password>\"}"

2. Copy `data.accessToken` from the response, then submit code:

curl.exe -X POST "%BACKEND_URL%/api/v1/code/upload" ^
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" ^
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <access-token>" ^
  --data-raw "{\"filename\":\"Example.java\",\"language\":\"java\",\"code\":\"class Example {}\"}"
